---
import Paper from '../layouts/Paper.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<Paper title="Privacy" description="Privacy policy for this website.">
  <article class="legal">
    <span class="label kicker">Privacy</span>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="note">
      English translation of the <a href={url('/de/datenschutz')}>German Datenschutzerklärung</a>. If the two
      differ, the German version applies.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      In short: no cookies, no analytics, no tracking, and no third-party embeds. Fonts are served from this
      site. The host, GitHub Pages, keeps standard server logs.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Controller</h2>
    <address>
      {site.name}<br />
      {site.address.street}<br />
      {site.address.postcode} {site.address.city}, {site.address.country.en}<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
    </address>

    <h2>2. Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies, uses no analytics or tracking tools, and embeds no third-party content.
      Fonts are served from this site, not from external providers.
    </p>
    <p>
      “Readers ask the Record” runs entirely in your browser. Questions you type are neither sent anywhere nor
      stored.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
    <p>
      This website is served by GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street,
      San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you visit, GitHub processes technically necessary data in server log
      files, in particular your IP address, the date and time of access, the page requested, the referrer URL,
      and browser and operating-system information.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is serving the website securely and
      reliably. Data may be transferred to the USA in the process. GitHub states that it is certified under
      the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework. For details, see
      <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Contact by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you email me, I process your details to answer your enquiry. Where it concerns possible work or
      employment, the legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR; otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. I delete the data once it
      is no longer needed for that purpose and no statutory retention obligations apply.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Links to other websites</h2>
    <p>
      This site links to external services such as LinkedIn and GitHub. These are plain links: no data is
      transferred until you click one. From then on, that provider’s privacy policy applies.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right of access (Art. 15 GDPR), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17), restriction of
      processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20), and to object to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR
      (Art. 21). To exercise them, write to the email address above.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also complain to a data protection supervisory authority, for example the State Commissioner for
      Data Protection and Freedom of Information of North Rhine-Westphalia (LDI NRW), Kavalleriestraße 2–4,
      40213 Düsseldorf, Germany.
    </p>

    <p class="updated">Last updated: October 2026</p>
    <p class="see-also"><a href={url('/impressum')}>Legal notice ›</a></p>
  </article>
</Paper>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 720px;
    padding: 32px 0;
  }

  h1 {
    font: 900 44px/1.1 var(--font-head);
    margin: 10px 0 12px;
  }

  h2 {
    font: 700 22px/1.25 var(--font-head);
    margin: 28px 0 8px;
  }

  p,
  address {
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    font-style: normal;
  }

  .note {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .updated {
    margin-top: 28px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .see-also {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
